# Generated by the coding-workflows validation harness. Do not edit.
#
# BuildKit reads <Dockerfile>.dockerignore next to the Dockerfile instead of
# the .dockerignore at the build context root. The harness builds
# Dockerfile.app from the repository root (`context: ..`) and copies it with
# `COPY . /workspace`, so a consumer's root .dockerignore written for its own
# images (for example `**` plus a few `!services/<name>/...` lines) would
# otherwise strip package.json and the rest of the project from /workspace.
#
# This file deliberately excludes nothing: the validation sandbox already
# stages only a screened copy of the tracked tree, so the whole staged copy
# belongs in the test image.
